These are exactly the hypotheses of `M5L.ResidualClasses_of_VFGen`; the group-exponent form adds
nothing on top of them (`rvGenCover_iff_rvIntCover`).  Henselianity enters only in the embedding
half (p3) and in the residue-field equality, neither of which the `Γ`/`RV` bookkeeping consumes.

Stress tests (following `QE/M5Ledger.lean` §11 and `QE/GammaDiv.lean` §6):
* (§4.i) the WLOG hypotheses are non-vacuous: `VFInvClosedOn_top`, `RVInvClosedOn_top`;
* (§4.ii) `RVGenCover ⊤ ⊤ ε` and `M5L.ResidualClasses S S` hold degenerately — the cover form is
  satisfiable and does not ask for new elements at the trivial point;
* (§4.iii) `M5L.Separated ⊤ e` is **false** for every new `e` (`not_separated_top`), so the
  separation hypothesis is a genuine restriction and not a tautology at the top;
* (§4.iv) the abstract sharpness of the WLOG: in `ℚ`, the submonoid `{q | 0 ≤ q}` is closed under
  division by every `n > 0` — the abstract content of `Assembly.GammaDivisible` — but is not closed
  under negation, so `RVInvClosedOn` is *not* a consequence of `Γ`-divisibility alone
  (`root_closed_not_neg_closed`).

No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`; `#print axioms` at the end.
